    ],
    "basis": "Seligman & Seligman 1932, p.206: limits stated in the text only. Quote: The Nuer inhabit the swamp region on either side of the White Nile south of its junction with the Bahr el Ghazal, extending southwards to about 7° 30' N, and eastwards to the Sobat.",
    "method": "Text-limit redraw. Only the limits stated on p.206 are used; no coordinate is invented. Named places from Wikidata P625. Rivers: Natural Earth 10m rivers/lake centrelines (White Nile, Bahr el Jebel, Sobat, Akobo); Baro: OpenStreetMap ways (ODbL). Projection for distances: local equirectangular at 9°N. Bank bands are 10 km each side or on the stated bank (EDITORIAL width; the pages give banks, not widths).",
